Wait — but on failure, cfg.Routes would be left partially set? Currently on failure in pass 1, cfg.Routes is partially filled. But ParseConfig returns nil config on failure anyway (`if f != nil return nil, f`). Actually ParseConfig: `if err := json.Unmarshal(data, &cfg); err != nil { ... return nil, ... }`. So cfg is discarded. Fine.

Hmm, but should I assign cfg.Routes only at the end after both passes succeed? Currently pass 1 assigns cfg.Routes[i] as it goes and pass 2 mutates. If UnmarshalJSON fails, json.Unmarshal returns error and ParseConfig returns nil. Behavior identical either way. Assigning at the end is cleaner.

